course: dictionary
lesson: 5481
title: Late: after the right time
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Late means after the right, usual or planned time. «You are late for school» means the bell has already rung when you walk in. Being on time is polite, and being late can make you miss the bus.
explain: Late can also mean near the end of a period of time, as in late at night or late in summer. Here the word tells you when something happens, not what time it is on a clock. Look at the words around it: night, summer or a clock time show you which meaning fits.
explain: Late has a polite meaning too. «Her late grandmother» means a grandmother who has died. The word changes its form: late, later, latest. When you meet late, ask yourself: is this about being on time, the end of a time, or someone who has died?
fact: Late means after the right, usual or planned time.
fact: «Late at night» means near the end of the day, when it is dark.
fact: «See you later» means goodbye for now, and «à plus» is the French way to say it.
fact: «Of late» means recently, and «at the latest» means no later than.
fact: In a time problem, «20 minutes late» means you add 20 minutes to the planned time.
exercise: «You are late for school.» What does late mean here? | Very quickly | *After the right time | Near the end of the day | Having died
exercise: «We stayed up late at night to watch the stars.» What does late mean here? | *Near the end of the day, when it is dark | Having died | After the right time | Quickly
exercise: A train is 20 minutes late. The planned arrival time is 10:00. What time does it actually arrive? | 11:00 | 9:40 | 10:00 | *10:20
test: «Her late grandmother loved gardening.» What does late mean here? | Very fast | Near the end of summer | After the right time | *Having died
test: In French, «à plus» means see you later. Which word means hello? | Bonne nuit | Merci | *Bonjour | Au revoir
exam: Which sentence uses late to mean near the end of a period of time? | The bus was late again, so we missed the start | Her late grandmother lived in Spain | *We walked home late in the evening | Ahmed was late for his football match
